# Internationalization

AttentionX uses **one locale catalog** (`public/locales/*.json`) for both the
extension UI and the X content script. Interpolation is `{param}` everywhere.

## Popup / onboarding / prompt / shared React UI

- Strings live in `public/locales/*.json` (flat dot-keys, e.g. `wizard.title`)
- Runtime: `@lib/i18n.js` (`initI18n()` then `t('key')` / `t('key', { count })`)
- Supported languages: `en`, `es`, `pt`, `de`, `fr`, `it` (see `SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES`)
- Add the same key to **every** locale file under `public/locales/` when introducing copy
- Prefer `t()` for new user-facing strings; do not mass-migrate existing hardcoded English unless you are already editing that component

## Content script (X Shadow DOM UI)

- Same catalog: `content.*` keys in `public/locales/*.json`
- Runtime: `src/content/i18n` (`t('content.card.trust')`)
- First paint uses embedded English in `src/content/i18n/fallback-en.ts`, then
  loads `locales/{lang}.json` via `chrome.runtime.getURL` and re-paints if needed
- Language: X.com UI (`html[lang]` / `lang` cookie), else `navigator.language`, else `en`
- Danish content strings live in `public/locales/da.json` (content keys; optional for popup)
- Keep `CONTENT_EN` identical to `content.*` in `en.json` — `src/i18n/resources.test.ts` enforces this
- Keep the content script as a self-contained IIFE via `vite.content.config.ts`

## Legacy / avoid for new work

- `src/App.tsx` + `src/i18n/resources.ts` + `react-i18next` — unused legacy shell
- Root `locales/*.json` duplicates `public/locales/`; **`public/locales/` is the runtime source**

## General rules

- Do not localize protocol values, event kinds/tags, URLs, storage keys, relay addresses, or log identifiers
- Use interpolation for counts and runtime values instead of string concatenation
- Cockpit pages and some panels (e.g. `AttentionXPanel`) still have hardcoded English — treat as migration debt; localize incrementally when touching that code
- When adding content-page copy: update `public/locales/en.json`, `fallback-en.ts`, and every other locale that should translate it (`da.json` at minimum for Danish)
